      "body": "## Motivation\n\nBaichuan2-13B / Baichuan-13B use ALiBi and skip RoPE. `baichuan.py` passes the ALiBi slopes to attention only on NPU, so on XPU the model runs with no position information and degenerates (`0 0 0 ...`). Baichuan2-13B-Chat gsm8k is **0.00** on B60 (vLLM RTX 6000 Blackwell: 53.5).\n\n## Modifications\n\n- **`models/baichuan.py`**: pass `slopes` on XPU too, as fp32.\n- **`layers/attention/xpu_backend.py`**: `forward_extend` / `forward_decode` accept `slopes` and forward it as `alibi_slopes` to `flash_attn_with_kvcache`, next to the existing `sinks` kwarg.\n\nOther models and backends are unchanged. On XPU with `--attention-backend triton`, Baichuan-13B now raises at the first forward (triton takes no `slopes`) instead of running without position information.\n\nDepends on sgl-project/sgl-kernel-xpu#573 (`alibi_slopes` in the FMHA kernels) and the sgl-kernel-xpu pin bump that follows it.\n\n## Accuracy Tests\n\nBaichuan2-13B-Chat, tp2, `--attention-backend intel_xpu`, gsm8k 5-shot, B60:\n\n| | docs | flexible | strict |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| main | 50 | 0.00 | 0.00 |\n| this PR | 50 | 0.52 | 0.52 |\n| this PR | 1319 | **0.5474** | **0.5459** |\n\nReference: vLLM RTX 6000 Blackwell 53.5, paper 56.8 (4-shot).\n\n```\npython -m sglang.launch_server --model-path baichuan-inc/Baichuan2-13B-Chat --trust-remote-code \\\n  --attention-backend intel_xpu --tp-size 2\n```\n\n## Speed Tests and Profiling\n\nNo speed impact on other models; the slopes are only passed for ALiBi Baichuan on XPU.\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [x] Format your code according to the [Format code with pre-commit](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#format-code-with-pre-commit).\n- [ ] Add unit tests according to the [Run and add unit tests](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#run-and-add-unit-tests). Not added here: the kernel PR carries `test_alibi_attention`, and the model-level change is covered by the accuracy run above.\n- [ ] Update documentation according to [Write documentations](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#write-documentations). Not needed.\n- [x] Provide accuracy and speed benchmark results according to [Test the accuracy](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#test-the-accuracy) and [Benchmark the speed](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#benchmark-the-speed).\n- [x] Follow the SGLang code style [guidance](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#code-style-guidance).\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #41512013037](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/41512013037)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #41512013003](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/41512013003)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #41512013060](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/41512013060)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n\n> [!TIP]\n> Base CI only covers the core cases, and its workload may not exercise your change. Use `/rerun-test` to run the tests your change touches, or copy this prompt for an agent:\n>\n> ```text\n> Find the registered tests this PR affects and run them with /rerun-test, following https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/blob/main/.agents/skills/rerun-test/SKILL.md\n> ```\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
